---
// The Riviera section front.
//
// The subdomain is a resident's guide and a shortlist form. It does not
// carry the delivery record, because a resident already lives there. The
// hub reader has not moved in yet, so the useful thing is the count: how
// many of the seventy-five buildings are handed over, which phases are
// finished, and what the developer is still selling.
import VerticalLayout from "../../layouts/VerticalLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
import Faq from "@dst/ui/Faq.astro";

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "How big is Azizi Riviera?",
    a: "<strong>75</strong> mid- and high-rise buildings with approximately <strong>16,000</strong> residences, in MBR City. That makes it one of the largest single residential communities in Dubai by unit count.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it finished?",
    a: "Not as of the last thing Azizi published. On <strong>7 August 2025</strong> the developer put <strong>53 of the 75</strong> buildings as handed over — all of phases 1, 2 and 3, plus five buildings in phase 4 — with the remaining 22 scheduled up until <strong>Q2 2026</strong>. No completion announcement for those 22 has followed.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is still for sale from the developer?",
    a: "Three Riviera products appear on Azizi's own construction-updates listing: Riviera from <strong>AED 1.22 million</strong>, Riviera Beachfront from <strong>AED 1.26 million</strong>, and Riviera Rêve from <strong>AED 2.35 million</strong>.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the lagoon?",
    a: "A <strong>2.7 km</strong> swimmable crystal lagoon. Azizi describes the community as three districts: a retail boulevard, the lagoon walk with eateries and boutiques, and Les Jardins, a green social space.",
  },
];
---
<VerticalLayout
  vertical="riviera"
  current="/riviera/"
  prose
  title="Azizi Riviera in Dubai: how much of it is actually built"
  description="Seventy-five buildings, about 16,000 homes in Dubai's MBR City. Azizi put 53 of them as handed over in August 2025 and scheduled the rest to Q2 2026 — and has published nothing since."
  image="/riviera.jpg"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Azizi Riviera"
    title="Azizi Riviera in Dubai: how much of it is actually built"
    image="/riviera.jpg"
    imageAlt="Illustration of the Azizi Riviera promenade at night: lit low-rise blocks along a canal, palms and walkways at the water's edge."
  >
    <p class="lede">
      Riviera is not one building, it is <strong>75</strong> of them, holding
      roughly <strong>16,000</strong> homes. Which one you are being shown
      matters more than the brochure does: as of Azizi's last published
      count, <strong>53</strong> had been handed over and <strong>22</strong>
      had not.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The count, as the developer last gave it</h2>
    <p>
      On <strong>7 August 2025</strong> Azizi Developments announced that
      Riviera had entered its final stage of delivery: 53 of the 75 buildings
      handed over, comprising all of phases 1, 2 and 3 and five buildings in
      phase 4, with the remaining 22 scheduled for completion
      <strong>up until Q2 2026</strong>. The same statement dated the recent
      handovers building by building — Riviera 63 on 24 March, Riviera 61 on
      9 June, Riviera 67 on 1 July, Riviera 65 on 21 July.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is a developer being unusually specific, and it is worth taking at
      face value. It is also the most recent figure there is. Q2 2026 has
      passed; no announcement of the last 22 has followed it. The absence of a
      press release is not evidence that a building is late — but it does mean
      the only honest answer to "is Riviera finished" is a question back:
      <em>which building, and which phase</em>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the developer is still selling</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Product</th><th>Sizes</th><th>From</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Riviera</td><td>Studio, 1 &amp; 3 bedrooms</td><td>AED 1.22M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Riviera Beachfront</td><td>1 &amp; 2 bedrooms</td><td>AED 1.26M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Riviera Rêve</td><td>1 &amp; 3 bedrooms</td><td>AED 2.35M</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Three things are readable off that table. Riviera and Riviera Beachfront
      start within AED 40,000 of each other, so the waterfront address is not
      the premium the name implies at the entry rung. Rêve starts at nearly
      twice either, which places it as a different product rather than a
      better floor of the same one. And the gap between a resale flat in a
      handed-over phase 1 building and a developer unit in phase 4 is not a
      discount or a markup — it is two different transactions, one of which
      comes with a completed building.
    </p>

    <h2>Three districts, one of them the reason people move</h2>
    <p>
      Azizi describes Riviera as a retail boulevard, a lagoon walk on the
      shores of a <strong>2.7 km</strong> swimmable crystal lagoon, and
      Les Jardins, a green social space. The lagoon is the part that changes
      daily life rather than the marketing: it is the reason the promenade
      carries foot traffic in the evening, and the reason distance from it
      shows up in what a unit lets for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout>
    <p>
      Riviera buildings are numbered, and the number tells you the phase. When
      a listing says "Azizi Riviera" and nothing else, that is the missing
      fact, not a detail: phase 1 has been lived in for years, and part of
      phase 4 was a site when the last official count was published.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>In this section</h2>
    <p>
      What a landlord may legally raise your rent by, and where that number
      comes from, is on
      <a href="/riviera/rent/" title="What a landlord in Dubai may raise your rent by">the renting page</a>.
      Who may legally change virtual assets for you in Dubai is on
      <a href="/riviera/money/" title="Who is licensed to handle crypto in Dubai">the money page</a>.
      The day-to-day guide — where to eat, where to swim, which block is which —
      is a separate site at
      <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc" title="Azizi Riviera community guide">riviera.dst.llc</a>.
      Dubai's other communities are across
      <a href="/sections/" title="What DST covers in Dubai">the sections</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Faq items={faqItems} />

  <section class="container">
    <p class="source-note">
      Building count, residence count, handover totals, phase breakdown,
      per-building handover dates, the three districts and the 2.7 km lagoon:
      Azizi Developments, press release of 7 August 2025, read 22 September
      2026. Starting prices and unit mixes for Riviera, Riviera Beachfront and
      Riviera Rêve: Azizi Developments' construction-updates listing, read
      22 September 2026. DST is not affiliated with Azizi Developments.
      Nothing here is investment advice.
    </p>
  </section>
</VerticalLayout>
